-- title:
--   Diamond automorphism of the two-chart model of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of `LaurentSeries L` generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L58): for every prime $\ell$ the predicate `HeckeInputsOneAlong` over an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ at level $Mp$ and $\ell$, and for every $d$ coprime to $Mp$ both the existence of a diamond automorphism $\sigma$ of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ with `IsDiamondAut` and the existence of a base-changed automorphism over the algebraic closure realising `diamondAut (M * p) d`. Finally, let $d$ be a natural number (no coprimality with $Mp$ is assumed) and $\theta$ an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ agreeing, on Laurent expansions, with [`ModularCurve.baseChangeAut L (ModularCurve.diamondAut (M * p) d)`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L24). Then there exist a self-isomorphism $w$ of the scheme [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) — the pushout gluing the spectra of the integral closure `chartAlgFin` of $A[j]$ in $K$ and of `chartAlgInf`, the integral closure of $A[j^{-1}]$ — and a ring automorphism $\rho$ of `chartAlgFin A K j` such that $w$ and its inverse both compose with the structure morphism `modelTo` to `Spec A` to give `modelTo` again, $\rho$ acts on elements of `chartAlgFin A K j` as $\theta$ does in $K$, and the finite chart inclusion `ιFin` followed by $w$ equals `Spec.map` of $\rho$ followed by `ιFin`.
--
--   This realises the diamond automorphism $\langle d \rangle$ of $X_1(Mp)$ as an automorphism of the two-chart integral model over the discrete valuation ring $A$, compatible with the map to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and acting on the $j$-finite chart through the restriction of the base-changed diamond automorphism of the function field. It is the form in which $\langle d \rangle$ is fed to the analysis of the special fibre and its components, and to the transport of the automorphism across the Abel–Jacobi map and the relative Picard scheme.
